From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Thu, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] AERA: reconcile X6886 USB OTG hotplug from uevents

The mt6789 common fstab describes OTG as /usbotg with a sysfs wildcard
and voldmanaged subpartitions. AERA only drained disk uevents, never
serviced the socket from the native UI loop, looked up usb_otg without a
leading slash in the battery thread, and kept absent removable volumes
in storage/wipe lists.

Port the TWRP hotplug contract to AERA without its operation executor:
service uevents non-blockingly from the UI thread only when no backend
job/decrypt/NAS/plugin operation is active, handle disk and partition
events, resync from /sys/block after overflow/coldboot with bounded
250 ms retries, remove stale children, give wildcard children unique
mount points and OTG labels, avoid mounting during discovery, and filter
removable storage/wipe entries by presence.

